# Conversion note: Salt expressed as 2-4% of cabbage weight; fermentation terminates by preference. No numeric cabbage mass, pH or fixed finish time inferred.

::ingredients

(cabbage) 1 head
(sea salt) 2-4% of cabbage weight
(water, cold) as needed for rinsing
(water, optional) enough to cover cabbage if needed

::equipment

(glass jars) as needed
(lid) -OR- (airlock lid) -OR- (coffee filter)
(rubber band, if using coffee filter)

::instructions

(glass jars) <clean, as many as needed>
(cabbage) <chop or shred> <rinse, cold water>
    + (sea salt) <sprinkle>
    <knead, clean hands, ~10m, enough liquid to cover cabbage>
    <pack, glass jar, press beneath liquid>
Optional [
    (water) <add, enough to completely cover cabbage if needed>
]
(jar) <cover, tight lid or airlock lid or coffee filter secured with rubber band>
    <ferment, room temperature, preferably 60-70°F / 15-20°C, at least 2 weeks, until desired flavour and texture, burp daily if tight lid>
    <cover, tight lid when finished> <store, cold>

::story

Sauerkraut is a based lacto-fermented food that is healthy and has a long shelf live.

